  "authority": "CONTRACT.md (G0) > this package > code. The frozen Kernel ABI 1.0.0 is referenced by $ref and wins on any conflict (CONTRACT.md 2.9).",
  "evolution_rules": [
    "this package never edits or redefines a frozen ABI type; it references ABI schemas by $ref",
    "breaking change = new major (V2)",
    "unknown required field/enum fails closed (every object is additionalProperties:false)",
    "unknown optional data in `extensions` (ABI ExtensionMap, x-* keys)",
    "additive change (new optional field, new enum member, new ShellCommandV1.action, new surface, new action class) = minor bump (1.x.0)",
    "new error codes are additive; receivers treat an unknown code as denied"
  ],
  "kinds": {
    "type": "a CONTRACT.md section 3 type: schema_id + schema_version + extensions",
    "message": "a call body, result or tool shape exactly as CONTRACT.md sections 2 and 7 give it (no schema_id, no extensions); the three '... minus server fields' bodies keep their type's schema_id, schema_version and extensions"
  },
  "open_conflicts": [
    "extensions[\"os.v1\"] (CONTRACT.md 2.1, 2.2, 2.9): the frozen ABI ExtensionMap accepts only ^x-[a-z0-9_.-]+$ keys. CheckExtensionV1 and LeaseExtensionV1 define the fields but are not wired into PolicyCheckV1/LeaseV1.",
    "ReceiptChainV1.domain (CONTRACT.md 2.5, 5): the ABI fixes domain to the const allternit.receipt.v1 and schema_id to ^allternit\\.kernel\\.; per-kind domains (check, approval, ...) and allternit.os.* receipts cannot ride in ReceiptChainV1. AuditAppendBody.domain follows the ABI.",
    "Hash encoding: CONTRACT.md uses bare 64-hex (Sha256Hex); the ABI Q4 rule is sha256:<hex> (ContentHash). Kept as the contract states."
  ],
